    ],
    "status": "present",
    "value": "Implement fixed-capacity plate stacks, pushing into the leftmost nonfull stack and popping from the rightmost nonempty stack or a specified stack. The approach is: min-heap of nonfull stable stack indices and a rightmost nonempty pointer; enqueue only full-to-nonfull transitions. Its target cost is amortized O(log S) per update/O(calls) space. Treat the invariant underlying that approach as the reason each local update preserves the required result. Check it against an independent bounded reference before relying on large-domain constructions."
  },
